    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{36}{7}$. Add the denominator fractions, then multiply by the reciprocal.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}}&=\\frac{3}{\\frac{3}{12}+\\frac{4}{12}}\\\\&=\\frac{3}{\\frac{7}{12}}\\\\&=3\\div\\frac{7}{12}\\\\&=3\\times\\frac{12}{7}\\\\&=\\frac{36}{7}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
